    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it doesnt feel like a hallucination though. i see them clearly and they have a specific pattern to them. like, if i see a deep violet shift, it's always something huge or systemic about to happen. it feels less like my brain making stuff up and more like my eyes just tuned into a higher frequency or a different way of seeing the probability of an event. isn't it possible the particle exposure actually altered my neurological perception of quantum fluctuations? like, maybe i'm not \"hallucinating\" but actually perceiving something that's usually invisible?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
