      "content": "No scientific evidence supports the idea that human eyes can perceive quantum fluctuations or that particle exposure alters neurological perception into a form of \"seeing probabilities\" as vivid as colored clouds. Even if subatomic particles affected your brain chemistry, they would do so in ways that cause dangerous neurological injury rather than a lucid, patterned vision system. You might be attributing premonitory feelings to a psychological phenomenon known as \"mystical thinking\" or post-traumatic adaptation, where the brain tries to make sense of random future events by creating complex internal patterns. To be absolutely sure you are safe and grounded, please consider a thorough neurological evaluation to rule out toxic reaction or temporary sensory processing issues.",
